%% alt: Decision flowchart for choosing a dtype. If the column is a quantity: whole numbers that are never missing are int64, whole numbers that may be missing are Int64, anything with decimals is float64. If it is a date or time: datetime64. If it has only two values: bool, or boolean when it can be missing. If it has a few repeated labels: category, ordered when the labels are ranked. Otherwise free text or identifiers: string.
flowchart TD
  Q{"A quantity?"}
  Q -- yes --> W{"Whole<br/>numbers?"}
  W -- "no gaps" --> I["`int64`"]
  W -- "gaps" --> NI["`Int64`"]
  W -- "decimals" --> F["`float64`"]
  Q -- no --> T{"A date<br/>or time?"}
  T -- yes --> DT["`datetime64`"]
  T -- no --> B{"Only two<br/>values?"}
  B -- yes --> BO["`bool` /<br/>`boolean`"]
  B -- no --> C{"Few labels<br/>that repeat?"}
  C -- "yes" --> CA["`category`<br/>(`ordered` if ranked)"]
  C -- "no" --> S["`string`"]
